From ef29e958413f59ac6e41051dad826ac54bd8bc72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olof Sandell <83674246+osandell@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 11:04:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(termio): deliver SIGHUP to child on Darwin killpg EPERM
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

killPid() ignored the EPERM that killpg(pgid, SIGHUP) returns on macOS when
the child has started its own session via setsid (any interactive shell). The
group signal was never delivered, so closing a surface left the shell — and
its gitstatusd children — alive; they reparented to PID 1 and piled up as
orphans. Fall back to kill(pid, SIGHUP) so the shell still gets its signal,
runs its exit hooks, and reaps its descendants.

Also includes in-progress macOS terminal / tab-bar work (BaseTerminalController,
TerminalView, ZedTabBar, Ghostty.App, AGENTS.md).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
